  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "Unexpected medical bills can be a significant financial burden, especially if you are unable to cover them with your existing insurance coverage. Here are some warning signs that you may be facing unexpected medical bills:\n\n1. High medical bills: If your medical bills are significantly higher than what you expected, it could be a sign that you are facing unexpected medical expenses.\n\n2. Unusual charges: If you receive charges that are not covered by your insurance or are not typical for your medical condition, it could be a sign that you are facing unexpected medical expenses.\n\n3. Late payments: If you are receiving late payments for your medical bills, it could be a sign that you are facing unexpected medical expenses.\n\n4. High interest rates: If your medical bills have high interest rates, it could be a sign that you are facing unexpected medical expenses.\n\n5. Lack of communication: If you are not receiving communication from your healthcare provider or insurance company regarding your medical bills, it could be a sign that you are facing unexpected medical expenses.\n\nIf you are facing unexpected medical bills, it is important to take action to address them. You can contact your healthcare provider or insurance company to discuss your medical bills and see if there are any errors or discrepancies. You can also consider seeking legal advice to help you navigate the billing process and protect your rights.",
